  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A ball is thrown from the top of a building so that its height $h$ metres above the ground after $t\\ge0$ seconds is given by\n$$h=-5t^2+10t+15.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Sketch a graph of the function $h$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Downward-opening parabola through $(0,15)$, with vertex $(1,20)$ and ground intercept $(3,0)$.",
          "worked": "Find the intercepts:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5t^2+10t+15&=0\\\\t^2-2t-3&=0\\\\(t-3)(t+1)&=0\\\\t&=-1,3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe turning point is midway between these roots, at $t=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h(0)&=15\\\\h(1)&=-5(1)^2+10(1)+15\\\\h(1)&=20.\\end{align*}$$\nSketch the downward-opening parabola through $(0,15)$, with vertex $(1,20)$ and intercept $(3,0)$. The physical flight is $0\\le t\\le3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p21-q3-a-solution-diagram",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"flightRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"function series for the projectile height\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 21 p21-q3-a-solution-diagram; teacher page 337\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.1cm,y=0.15cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{flightRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (-0.25,0)--(4.1,0) node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,right] {$t\\text{ (s)}$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,-7)--(0,24) node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,above] {$h\\text{ (m)}$};\n\\draw[flightRed,line width=0.8pt,domain=0:3,samples=61] plot (\\x,{-5*\\x*\\x+10*\\x+15});\n\\draw[flightRed,dashed,line width=0.8pt,domain=3:3.3,samples=16] plot (\\x,{-5*\\x*\\x+10*\\x+15});\n\\fill[black] (0,15) circle (1pt) (1,20) circle (1pt) (3,0) circle (1pt);\n\\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,left] at (0,15) {$(0,15)$};\n\\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,above right] at (1,20) {$(1,20)$};\n\\node[fill=white,inner sep=1pt,below left] at (3,0) {$(3,0)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 21,
                "sourceRegion": "17H question 3(a); teacher PDF page 8, printed page 337",
                "description": "Complete labelled projectile sketch with downward concavity, initial point, turning point and ground intercept. Solid curve represents flight; dashed continuation represents the algebraic function after impact.",
                "mathematics": "h=-5t^2+10t+15 for t>=0; vertex (1,20), initial point (0,15), positive root (3,0).",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the initial height of the ball above ground level?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15\\text{ m}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}h(0)&=-5(0)^2+10(0)+15\\\\h(0)&=15.\\end{align*}$$\nThe initial height is $15\\text{ m}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "For how long is the ball in flight?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "At ground level, $h=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5t^2+10t+15&=0\\\\t^2-2t-3&=0\\\\(t-3)(t+1)&=0\\\\t&=3,-1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $t\\ge0$, the ball is in flight for $3\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "For what duration is the ball more than $15$ metres above ground level?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\text{ s}$.\n\nThe ball is above $15$ m for $0<t<2$.",
          "worked": "Find when the height equals $15$ m:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5t^2+10t+15&=15\\\\-5t^2+10t&=0\\\\-5t(t-2)&=0\\\\t&=0,2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola lies above $h=15$ between these times. Thus $0<t<2$, a duration of $2\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "What is the maximum height reached by the ball?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20\\text{ m}$.",
          "worked": "The turning point is midway between the roots $t=-1$ and $t=3$, so it occurs at $t=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}h(1)&=-5(1)^2+10(1)+15\\\\h(1)&=20.\\end{align*}$$\nThe maximum height is $20\\text{ m}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
